    mainDescription:
      "<p>Petaluma built its early economy on poultry and egg production, and the historic warehouse district along the Petaluma River still reflects that industrial past, now largely converted to creative office, flex, and small commercial space. The city's downtown mixes that adaptive-reuse stock with newer commercial development along the 101 corridor, giving exchange investors two distinct submarkets to choose from. Sitting between Marin's tighter growth boundaries and Sonoma County's wine country economy, Petaluma has developed a commercial identity that's genuinely its own rather than a smaller echo of either neighbor.</p>",
